From: royka1 <397414+royka1@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 21:33:16 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sm8450: Describe the CPU capacities

The CPU nodes carry no capacity-dmips-mhz, so arch_topology falls back
to 1024 for every CPU and the scheduler cannot tell a Cortex-A510 from
the Cortex-X2. A CPU-bound thread that starts on cpu0-3 stays there
for good, capped at the 2016 MHz ceiling of the little cluster, while
cpu7 idles: a 50M-iteration awk loop takes 7.6 s pinned to cpu0 and
1.5 s pinned to cpu7.

Add the per-MHz capacities of Qualcomm's downstream Waipio and Cape
DTBs, which are identical for both SoCs. With the maximum frequencies
the EPSS LUT reports on an SM8475 this yields cpu_capacity 277 for the
A510, 832 for the A710 and 1024 for the X2, so util-based load
balancing sees heavy tasks on the little cores as misfit and moves
them up.

dynamic-power-coefficient is left out on purpose: the CPU OPPs come
from the hardware LUT, and adding the coefficient would register an
energy model and turn on EAS, which is a separate decision.

Signed-off-by: royka1 <397414+royka1@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8450.dtsi | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

